course: dictionary
lesson: 8640
title: Seabirds of the coast
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A seabird is a bird that lives near the sea and gets most of its food from the sea. Gulls, puffins, terns and albatrosses are all seabirds.
explain: Look at the words around the word for clues. «Oil spills poison seas and coasts and kill seabirds, fish and other wildlife.» Seabirds are listed with fish and wildlife, so they are living things of the sea and coast.
explain: Phrases like «seabird colony» and «nesting seabirds» show that seabirds often gather and nest together on cliffs, rocks or islands. To check your meaning, put it into the sentence in place of the word: «Oil spills kill birds that live near the sea» still makes sense.
fact: A seabird is a bird that lives near the sea and finds most of its food in it.
fact: Seabirds often nest on cliffs, rocks or islands, and they can fly far over the water.
fact: A «seabird colony» is a large group of seabirds nesting together in one place.
fact: Krill are tiny shrimp-like animals that feed whales, seals, penguins, fish and seabirds.
fact: If you find a dead or sick bird, do not touch it. Tell an adult, who can report it.
exercise: What is a seabird? | A bird that lives only in cities and parks | A fish that swims in the sea | A sea animal with no wings | *A bird that lives near the sea and finds most of its food in it
exercise: Which of these is a seabird? | *Puffin | Robin | Sparrow | Pigeon
exercise: «Oil spills poison seas and coasts and kill seabirds, fish and other wildlife.» What happens to the seabirds in this sentence? | They are fed by the oil | They turn into fish | They build new nests on the coast | *They are harmed and die
test: Where do seabirds often nest? | In the middle of towns | *On cliffs, rocks or islands | In deep caves under the ground | Inside houses
test: What is a «seabird colony»? | *A large group of seabirds nesting together | A seabird that cannot fly | A group of fish swimming together | A type of boat
exam: A child finds a sick seabird on the beach. What should they do? | *Do not touch it, and tell an adult who can report it | Pick it up and take it home | Ignore it, because birds always get better by themselves | Feed it some chips to make it strong
